Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 29 at 7:13PM MDT until October 1 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The Southeast Mountains, the Wet Mountain Valley, eastern\nFremont county and the southeast plains.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rainfall associated with a remnant tropical\nstorm system will spread across southern Colorado through\nThursday.\n\n- The Southeast Mountains, including the Aspen Acres burn area, the\nWet Mountain Valley, eastern Fremont county, and the southeast\nplains.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-01T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains Between 8500 And 11000 Ft; Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains above 11000 Ft; Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Between 7500 and 11000 Ft; Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Above 11000 Ft; Northwestern Fremont County  Above 8500Ft; Western/Central Fremont County Below 8500 Ft; Wet Mountain Valley Below 8500 Ft; Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft; Canon City Vicinity/Eastern Fremont County; Northern El Paso County/Monument Ridge/Rampart Range Below 7500 Ft; Colorado Springs Vicinity/Southern El Paso County/Rampart Range Below 7400 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft; Crowley County; La Junta Vicinity/Otero County; Eastern Las Animas County; Western Kiowa County; Eastern Kiowa County; Las Animas Vicinity/Bent County; Lamar Vicinity/Prowers County; Springfield Vicinity/Bac